        "Wudu is the spiritual and physical purification required before standing in prayer.\n\nThe Quran establishes four obligatory pillars (Fara'id) in Surah Al-Ma'idah (5:6):\n1. Washing the face from forehead to chin and ear to ear.\n2. Washing both arms including the elbows.\n3. Wiping at least a quarter of the head with wet hands (Hanafi; Sunnat is wiping the whole head).\n4. Washing both feet up to and including the ankles.\n\nProphetic Sunnahs (Recommended Practices):\n- Starting with Bismillah and intention (Niyyah) in the heart.\n- Washing the hands thrice up to wrists.\n- Rinsing the mouth (Madmadah) and cleaning the nose (Istinshaq) thrice.\n- Running wet fingers through the beard and between fingers and toes (Takhlil).\n- Maintaining sequential order (Tartib) without prolonged interruption (Muwalat)." to "Alwala ita ce tsarkakewar ruhi da ta zahiri da ake bukata kafin a tsaya a cikin sallah.\n\nAlqur'ani ya kafa rukunan farilla guda hudu (Fara'id) a cikin suratu Al-Ma'idah (5:6):\n1. Wanke fuska tun daga goshi zuwa gabo da kunne zuwa kunne.\n2. Wanke hannu biyu ciki har da gwiwar hannu.\n3. Shafa akalla kashi daya bisa hudu na kai da jikakkun hannu (Hanafi; Sunnatu tana shafa kan gaba daya).\n4. Wanke ƙafafu biyu har zuwa idon sawu.\n\nSunnan Annabi (Ayyukan da aka Shawarta):\n- Farawa da Bismillah da Niyya (Niyyah) a cikin zuciya.\n- Wanke hannu sau uku har zuwa wuyan hannu.\n-Kurkure baki (Madmadah) da tsaftace hanci (Istinshaq) sau uku.\n- Gudun rigar yatsu ta gemu da tsakanin yatsu da yatsu (Takhlil).\n- Kula da tsari (Tartib) ba tare da tsawaita lokaci mai tsawo ba (Muwalat).",
        "Khushu' is inner humility, stillness of the limbs, and attentive contemplation of what one is reciting.\n\nPractical Anchors for Khushu':\n- Prepare before the Takbir: Perform wudu mindfully, arrive before iqamah, and eliminate immediate physical distractions.\n- Contemplate the Words: Recite slowly (Tartil). When saying 'Al-Hamdu lillahi Rabbil-Alameen', remember Allah responds directly: 'My servant has praised Me' (Sahih Muslim 395).\n- Fix the Gaze: Direct your gaze respectfully at the place of prostration (Sujud), rather than looking around.\n- Remember the Final Prayer: The Prophet (peace be upon him) advised: 'Pray as if it were your farewell prayer' (Sunan Ibn Majah 4171)." to "Khushu'i shi ne tawali'u na ciki, da nutsuwar gabobi, da lura da abin da mutum yake karantawa.\n\nAnchors na aiki don Khushu':\n- Shiri kafin Takbir: Ku yi alwala da hankali, ku isa gabanin iqama, da kawar da shagaltuwar jiki nan take.\n- Yi la'akari da Kalmomin: Karanta a hankali (Tartil). Lokacin da kake cewa 'Al-Hamdu lillahi Rabbil-Alameen', ka tuna cewa Allah yana amsawa kai tsaye: 'Bawana ya yabe ni' (Sahih Muslim 395).\n- Ka gyara Kallon: Ka mayar da kallonka cikin girmamawa ga wurin Sujuda, maimakon kalle-kalle.\n- Ku Tuna Sallar Karshe: Annabi (SAW) ya yi nasiha da cewa: “Ku yi Sallah kamar Sallar bankwana” (Sunan Ibn Majah 4171).",
        "The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: 'Jibril kept enjoining good treatment of the neighbor upon me until I thought he would assign him a share of inheritance.' (Sahih al-Bukhari 6014).\n\nIslamic teachings identify three classes of neighbors:\n1. A neighbor who is a relative and Muslim: has three rights (kinship, Islam, neighborhood).\n2. A neighbor who is Muslim: has two rights (Islam and neighborhood).\n3. A neighbor of different faith: has the sacred right of good neighborhood and kindness.\n\nHarm to neighbors is strictly condemned: 'By Allah he does not believe... whose neighbor is not safe from his harm.' (Sahih al-Bukhari 6016)." to "Annabi Muhammad (saw) ya ce: \"Jibrilu ya kasance yana yi min wasiyya da kyautatawa makwabci har sai da na yi tunanin zai ba shi rabon gado.\" (Sahihul Bukhari 6014).\n\nKoyarwar Musulunci ta bayyana nau'o'i uku na makwabta:\n1. Makwabci dan uwa musulmi: yana da hakki guda uku ('yan uwa, Musulunci, unguwa).\n2. Makwabci musulmi: yana da hakki guda biyu (Musulunci da unguwa).\n3. Makwabcin imani daban-daban: yana da hakki mai tsarki na kyakkyawan unguwa da kyautatawa.\n\nAn hukunta cutar da maƙwabta: 'Wallahi bai yi imani ba... wanda maƙwabcinsa bai aminta daga cutarwarsa ba.' (Sahihul Bukhari 6016).",
